@startuml fig1_system_view
' Diagram 1 of the ISO/IEC 22989 pattern: the system, its tasks and its
' functions.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: the first of the three views the pattern is built in. What an
' AI system is made of, what it is for, and which activities of the life cycle
' it performs.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - algorithms, models and parameters: diagram 2
'  - data and the processes preparing it: diagram 3
'  - the qualities of clause 3.5: diagram 4
'
' Control appears here among the functions. Its entry sits in clause 3.5 among
' the terms related to trustworthiness, but the definition says action, which
' is what the other functions are as well.
'  - Retraining and MachineLearning below Training, which belong to the
'    algorithmic view and appear in diagram 2
'
' Read top to bottom: the system, what it addresses, what it does.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 42
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

' ===================================================================
'  The system and what it is made of
' ===================================================================

class AISystem
class AIComponent

class AIType
class SymbolicAI
class SubsymbolicAI

class SystemDesign {
  <<enum>>
  Cloud
  Edge
  Hybrid
}

AIType <|-- SymbolicAI
AIType <|-- SubsymbolicAI

AISystem --> "*" AIComponent  : consistsOf
AISystem --> "*" AIType       : hasType
AISystem --> "1" SystemDesign : hasDesign

' ===================================================================
'  What the system is for
' ===================================================================

class Task
class Classification
class Regression
class Clustering
class Generation
class Prediction

Task <|-- Classification
Task <|-- Regression
Task <|-- Clustering
Task <|-- Generation

AISystem   --> "*" Task : hasTask
Prediction --> "1" Task : fulfilsTask

' ===================================================================
'  What the system does
' ===================================================================

class AIFunction
class Acquisition
class Storing
class DataProcessing
class Training
class Validation
class Verification
class Evaluation
class Inference
class Control

AIFunction <|-- Acquisition
AIFunction <|-- Storing
AIFunction <|-- DataProcessing
AIFunction <|-- Training
AIFunction <|-- Validation
AIFunction <|-- Verification
AIFunction <|-- Evaluation
AIFunction <|-- Inference
AIFunction <|-- Control

' The same relation runs from both. The edge from the system passes the
' AIComponent box on its way down, so its label was landing on top of that box.
' Labelling the shorter edge instead puts the name where the relation is
' readable, and the long edge carries the multiplicity alone.
AISystem    --> "*" AIFunction
AIComponent --> "*" AIFunction : hasFunction
Inference   --> "*" Prediction : creates

' Layout only: keep each fan of siblings on one row.
Acquisition -[hidden]right- Storing
Storing     -[hidden]right- DataProcessing
DataProcessing -[hidden]right- Training
Training    -[hidden]right- Validation
Validation  -[hidden]right- Verification
Verification -[hidden]right- Evaluation
Evaluation  -[hidden]right- Inference
Inference   -[hidden]right- Control

Classification -[hidden]right- Regression
Regression     -[hidden]right- Clustering
Clustering     -[hidden]right- Generation

SymbolicAI -[hidden]right- SubsymbolicAI

@enduml
